=== 3. The two ends of the scale ===
  Sex (forty-five pairs): median +0.2190, range +0.0389 to +0.6470, median sign concordance 0.5528
    same platform, 18 pairs: median +0.2686 | cross-platform, 27 pairs: median +0.2017
  Disease (five within-disease pairs): Parkinson +0.0430; Schizophrenia +0.0713; Alzheimer +0.0026; Depression -0.0089; IBD +0.1174
  Disease (forty cross-disease pairs): median +0.0068, maximum +0.0484

  Interpretation: sex, a truly shared exposure, gives concordance of the above magnitude under the same criterion, in the same cohorts and
  across platforms and populations. The cross-disease concordance of disease is far below it, so 'not detectable'
  is not a property of this design.

